<title>FRANCE: Technip wins ammonia plant contract.</title>
<headline>Technip wins ammonia plant contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>French industrial installations group Technip said on Thursday it had signed a contract with Wesfarmers CSBP for the construction of an ammonia plant in Australia worth about U.S. $100 million.</p>
<p>The contract was awarded to Technipetrol.</p>
<p>The plant at Kwinana, near Perth in western Australia, will produce 650 tons of ammonia daily, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said construction was scheduled for completion in the third quarter of 1999.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
